          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Thunderbird and Firefox. The Mozilla Foundation's Security Advisory describes the following issue:\nMemory safety bugs are present in the following versions: Firefox ESR 115.26, Firefox ESR 128.13, Thunderbird ESR 128.13, Firefox ESR 140.1, Thunderbird ESR 140.1, Firefox 141, and Thunderbird 141. Some of these bugs showed evidence of memory corruption, and we presume that with enough effort, some of these could have been exploited to run arbitrary code.",
